  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>bodeoptions</keyword>
  <short_description>Options for a Bode plot.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>opt = bodeoptions()</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>opt</param_name>
      <param_description
      >a structure holding the Bode plot options.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p><b>opt = bodeoptions()</b> returns a structure holding the Bode plot options with their default values.</p>
    <p>The returned structure can be passed to <b>bodeplot</b> to customize the rendering. The honored fields are:</p>
    <p><b>PhaseUnits</b>: <b>'deg'</b> (default) or <b>'rad'</b>.</p>
    <p><b>Grid</b>: <b>'off'</b> (default) or <b>'on'</b>.</p>
    <p>Additional fields (<b>FreqUnits</b>, <b>MagUnits</b>, <b>Title</b>, <b>XLabel</b>, <b>YLabel</b>) are provided with default values so that assignment does not error.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography />
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data
        runnable="cli"
      ><![CDATA[opt = bodeoptions();
opt.PhaseUnits = 'rad';
opt.Grid = 'on'
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
